==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*10 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*5 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*3 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Primeval Cyclone]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Chickful A]]s spawn, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
**3 [[Corporal Weyland]]s spawn, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage is balanced around [[Cats of the Cosmos|CotC]] Chapter 3 completion with the massive strength magnifications on those nasty [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]], so max all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] before attempting.

The strategy in this stage is to focus the backliner enemies as much as possible before killing the Primeval Cyclone. [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|LD units]] such as [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]], [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]], and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]], along with [[Wave Attack]] units like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] can accomplish this task. Depending on how you approach this stage, a Fiend Cat with Target Angel Talent can make this stage easier or harder. Talented [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] can easily help keep the Primeval Cyclone from destroying your LD stack. A general lineup may consist of 3 meatshields, Rodeo Cat, and 6 LD/Wave Attack units. It may help to replace some of the LD/Wave Attack units with long-ranged units in case the Primeval Cyclone dies before you can finish off the rest of the backliner enemies.

Angels and Starred Aliens appear as support, so if you have any remaining slots, you may add in anti-Angels and anti-Aliens if you want. Do note that this is not necessary and only add them if you have nothing else to add to your Cat army.

If you struggle with the Primeval Cyclone itself, it may be advisable to focus on taking it down first, as doing so will allow you to face the Angel backliners more safely. If taking this approach to the stage, [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] will be your best friend here. At level 50, their health becomes high enough to survive an additional hit from Corporal Weyland. Lower levels should suffice, but a highly boosted Slapsticks may help if you are still struggling. With Talents they gain the ability to [[Weaken|weaken]] the cyclone as additional crowd-control.

Once the Primeval Cyclone is taken care of, the fight becomes a battle of attrition. Your goal here is to whittle down the health of the Angels with midrange attackers while not losing much ground. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] are great for support, and allow you to stall or even regain distance from the assortment of backliners. It may take a while, but you should eventually emerge victorious.

